      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Annex 6 answers frequently asked questions about interferon-gamma release assays (IGRAs) for TB infection, including the two commercial tests WHO reviewed in 2017. It explains that IGRAs measure interferon-gamma released by white blood cells exposed to M. tuberculosis-specific antigens absent from BCG strains, and that like TST they cannot separate infection from disease. It also covers specimen handling, interpretation and how to handle discordant or borderline results.",
